{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:a4e8ca3fc2df04ed","name":"Eetoa Ro","source":{"id":"source:reference-a4e8ca3fc2df04ed","title":"Eetoa Ro","revision":21566,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T02:02:40Z","sha256":"a016d17129f88eb26c769ac47b973c2e7b255708937dd15eb8ac8907d5f8202d","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21566","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Eetoa%20Ro&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-a4e8ca3fc2df04ed","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dawn of Defiance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dawn_of_Defiance"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["The Core of Corruption"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Core_of_Corruption","referenceId":"reference:16e354d31389fcca"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Although only in his late teens, the fast-talking, self-confident Eetoa is enormously street smart and has vast knowledge of the Works underworld. If the heroes negotiate successfully, they may use him as an additional contact in their investigations, though he knows much less about areas outside of the Works.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Eetoa may be reached by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Comlink"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Comlink","referenceId":"reference:609e72c37493843f"}," to arrange a meeting. He directs the heroes to the landing platform of the Galaxy IV Coolant Refinery, which has been abandoned for decades. When they arrive at the large, rusty platform, Eetoa appears from behind decrepit equipment and zips up to them on an unarmed, banged-up ",{"tag":"a","children":["74-Z Speeder Bike"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/74-Z_Speeder_Bike","referenceId":"reference:5f212506c0af4f6a"},". He wears a red and blue flight suit that is faded and torn. He negotiates from the speeder bike while the engine is running. If he feels threatened, he zips off at high speed, using his knowledge of the area to lose his pursuers in the refinery's tangled pipes and passageways.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Eetoa realizes that he may be outmatched by the heroes and uses ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Fool's Luck"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fool%27s_Luck"}]}," at the beginning of the encounter, applying an additional +5 to all ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Checks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Checks"},". He reserves ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knack"}]}," for negotiating payment.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Eetoa is cashing in on both sides. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Resh"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Resh","referenceId":"reference:a1201bc5a196b63e"}," is paying him to arrange passage off the planet; however, Eetoa also charges the heroes 5,000 credits (starting) for information. His ",{"tag":"a","children":["Attitude"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attitude"}," begins as Indifferent. He tells them that ",{"tag":"a","children":["Resh"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Resh","referenceId":"reference:a1201bc5a196b63e"}," needs a way off the planet, and if the heroes convince Eetoa that they can help (and pay the fee), he gives them Resh's location at a warehouse hideout deep within the Works Labyrinth. For an additional 500 credits, he'll also let them know that bounty hunters are looking for Resh.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Eetoa Ro Statistics (CL 4)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrel","referenceId":"reference:316d580fd4c35ecc"}," 4\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 3; ",{"tag":"b"